 515  *==============================================================================
 516  * 2. Calibration of variables
 517  *==============================================================================
 518   
 519  Parameter
 520  *==============================================================================
 521  *  2.1 Variables in GTAP DB
 522  *==============================================================================
 523  * These are the variables from GTAP DB format 6 verion used in the calibration process.
 524  * Population data is in million while all other data are expressed in millions of USD
 525   
 526   EVOS(endw,acts,reg)            Endowments at agents prices
 527   FBEP(endw,acts,reg)            Factor-based subsidies
 528   FTRV(endw,acts,reg)            Taxes - Factor Employment Tax Revenue
 529   MFRV(comm,reg,reg)             Protection MFA export subsidy equivalent
 530   OSEP(comm,reg)                 Ordinary output subsidies
 531   POP(reg)                       Population
 532   TFRV(comm,reg,reg)             Protection Ordinary Import Duty
 533   VDEP(reg)                      Capital Stock Value of Depreciation
 534   VDFP(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Dom Purchases at Agent Prices
 535   VDFB(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Dom Purchases at Mkt Prices
 536   VMFP(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Imp Purchases at Agent Prices
 537   VMFB(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Imp Purchases at Mkt Prices
 538   VDGP(comm,reg)                 Government Dom Purchases at Agents Prices
 539   VDGB(comm,reg)                 Government Dom Purchases at Market Prices
 540   VDPP(comm,reg)                 Private Hhold Dom Purchases at Agents Prices
 541   VDPB(comm,reg)                 Private Hhold Dom Purchases at Market Prices
 542   EVFB(endw,acts,reg)            Endowments Firms Purchases at Market Prices
 543   VIFA(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Imports at Agents Prices
 544   VIFM(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Imports at Market Prices
 545   VMGP(comm,reg)                 Government Imports at Agents Prices
 546   VMGB(comm,reg)                 Government Imports at Market Prices
 547   VMSB(comm,reg,reg)             Trade Bilateral Imports at Market Prices
 548   VMPP(comm,reg)                 Private Households Imports at Agents Prices
 549   VMPB(comm,reg)                 Private Households Imports at Market Prices
 550   VCIF(comm,reg,reg)             Trade Bilateral Imports at World Prices
 551   VKB(reg)                       Capital Stock Value at Beginning-of-Period
 552   VST(marg,reg)                  Trade Exports Internatl Trans Mkt Prices
 553   VTMFSD(marg,comm,reg,reg)      Trade Margins Internatl Trans World Prices
 554   VXSB(comm,reg,reg)             Trade Bilateral Exports at Market Prices
 555   VFOB(comm,reg,reg)             Trade Bilateral Exports at World Prices
 556   XTRV(comm,reg,reg)             Protection Ordinary Export Subsidy
 557   VDIP(comm,reg)                 Investment expenditure on dom. c in r at producer prices
 558   VMIP(comm,reg)                 Investment expenditure on imp. c in r at producer prices
 559   VDIB(comm,reg)                 Investment expenditure on dom. c in r at basic prices
 560   VMIB(comm,reg)                 Investment expenditure on imp. c in r at basic prices
 561   MAKES(comm,acts,reg)           Make matrix valued at suppliers prices
 562   MAKEB(comm,acts,reg)           Make matrix valued at basic prices
 563   
 564  *==============================================================================
 565  *  2.2 Variables in the aggregated model
 566  *==============================================================================
 567   CO(i,z)         Household consumption of commodity I
 568   CGO(i,z)        Public final consumption of commodity i
 569   INVO(i,z)       Final demand of commodity i for investment purposes
 570   DDO(i,z)        Demand for domestic production of commodity i
 571   DEPO(z)         Depreciation
 572   DIO(i,j,z)      Intermediate consumption of commodity i by industry j
 573   DSO(j,i,z)      Supply of commodity i by sector j to the domestic market
 574   EXO(i,z,zj)     Exports supply of commodity i from country z to country zj
 575   EXTO(i,z)       Total Export
 576   IMO(i,zj,z)     Imports of commodity m by country z from country zj
 577   RKDO(k,j,z)     Type k capital income in industry j
 578   RKDO_J(k,z)     Type k capital income
 579   KSTO(z)         Total capital stock in region z
 580   LDO(l,j,z)      Industry j demand for labour l
 581   LDO_J(l,z)      Demand for labour l
 582   MRGNO(i,z)      Demand for commodity i as a margin
 583   POPO(z)         Population
 584   TDHO(z)         Household income taxes
 585   DTAX(f,z)       Direct taxes
 586   TICO(i,z)       Government receipts of indirect taxes on commodity i
 587   TIKO(k,j,z)     Government receipts of indirect taxes on capital k of industry j
 588   TIKO_J(k,z)     Government receipts of indirect taxes on capital k
 589   TIMO(i,zj,z)    Government receipts of indirect taxes on imports of commodity i
 590   TIPO(j,z)       Government receipts of indirect taxes on production of industry j
 591   TIWO(l,j,z)     Government receipts of indirect taxes on wages and salaries of industry j
 592   TIWO_J(l,z)     Government receipts of indirect taxes on wages and salaries
 593   TIXO(i,z,zj)    Government receipts of indirect taxes on exports of commodity i
 594   tmrg(i,ij,zj,z) Rate of commodity i margin applied to import m from country zj
 595   XSO_I(i,z)      total production by commodity
 596   XSO(j,i,z)      Industry j production of commodity i
 597   XSTO(j,z)       Total aggregate output of industry j
 598   tssm(i,j,z)     Intermediate tax by source import
 599   tssd(i,j,z)     Intermediate tax by source domestic
 600   MAKE(j,i,z)     Make matrix valued at basic prices
 601   DSO_I(i,z)      Supplys of domestic production of commodity i
 602   XSO_I(i,z)      Total aggregate output of commoity i
 603   TotalCost(j,z)  Total Cost by industry
 604  ;
 605   
 606  *==============================================================================
 607  *  2.3 Loading parameters from GTAP database
 608  *==============================================================================
--- LOAD  EVOS = 13:EVOS
--- LOAD  FBEP = 40:FBEP
--- LOAD  FTRV = 41:FTRV
--- LOAD  MFRV = 46:MFRV
--- LOAD  OSEP = 43:OSEP
--- LOAD  POP = 42:POP
--- LOAD  TFRV = 45:TFRV
--- LOAD  VDEP = 31:VDEP
--- LOAD  VDFP = 11:VDFP
--- LOAD  VDFB = 9:VDFB
--- LOAD  VDGP = 20:VDGP
--- LOAD  VDGB = 18:VDGB
--- LOAD  VMFP = 12:VMFP
--- LOAD  VMFB = 10:VMFB
--- LOAD  MAKES = 16:MAKES
--- LOAD  MAKEB = 17:MAKEB
--- LOAD  VDPP = 24:VDPP
--- LOAD  VDPB = 22:VDPB
--- LOAD  EVFB = 14:EVFB
--- LOAD  VDIP = 28:VDIP
--- LOAD  VDIB = 26:VDIB
--- LOAD  VMIP = 29:VMIP
--- LOAD  VMIB = 27:VMIB
--- LOAD  VMGP = 21:VMGP
--- LOAD  VMGB = 19:VMGB
--- LOAD  VMPP = 25:VMPP
--- LOAD  VMPB = 23:VMPB
--- LOAD  VMSB = 35:VMSB
--- LOAD  VCIF = 34:VCIF
--- LOAD  VKB = 39:VKB
--- LOAD  VST = 36:VST
--- LOAD  VTMFSD = 38:VTMFSD
--- LOAD  VXSB = 32:VXSB
--- LOAD  VFOB = 33:VFOB
--- LOAD  XTRV = 44:XTRV
 612   
 613  *==============================================================================
 614  * 2.4 Mapping between variables in the model and GTAP
 615  *==============================================================================
 616  *==============================================================================
 617  * 2.4.1 Households consumption
 618  *==============================================================================
 619  * Households consumption is given by the sum of domestic purchases at
 620  * agents prices (VDPP) and private household imports at agents prices (VMPP).
 621   
 622   CO(i,z)         = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 623                         VDPP(comm,reg)+VMPP(comm,reg)};
 624   
 625   CO(i,z)$(CO(i,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 626   
 627  *==============================================================================
 628  * 2.4.2 Public final consumption
 629  *==============================================================================
 630  * Public final consumption is given by the sum of domestic purchases at
 631  * agents prices (VDGP) and public final imports at agents prices (VMGP).
 632   
 633   CGO(i,z)        = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 634                         VDGP(comm,reg)+VMGP(comm,reg)};
 635   
 636   CGO(i,z)$(CGO(i,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 637   
 638  *==============================================================================
 639  * 2.4.3 Demand for investment purposes
 640  *=============================================================================
 641  *  In the GTAP data, the accumulation account is presented in the
 642  *  production sector CGDS (Capital goods). Demand for investment purposes
 643  *  is thus given by the sum of domestic purchases at agents prices (VDIP)
 644  *  and public final imports at agents prices (VMIP) for this sector.
 645   
 646   INVO(i,z)       = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 647                        VDIP(comm,reg)+VMIP(comm,reg)};
 648   
 649   INVO(i,z)$(INVO(i,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 650   
 651  *==============================================================================
 652  * 2.4.4 Intermediate demand
 653  *==============================================================================
 654  * Intermediate consumption is given by the sum of domestic purchases at
 655  * agents prices (VDFP) and public final imports at agents prices (VMFP).
 656   
 657   DIO(i,j,z)      = SUM[(comm,acts,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 658                        $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 659                        VDFP(comm,acts,reg)+VMFP(comm,acts,reg)];
 660   
 661   DIO(ene,j2,z)$(DIO(ene,j2,z) lt 0.1) = sum(enee,DIO(enee,j2,z))*0.015 ;
 662   DIO(i,j,z)$(DIO(i,j,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 663   
 664  * for data balancing
 665  * DIO(i,'09_PAPERPRO','05_MNG')$(DIO(i,'09_PAPERPRO','05_MNG') lt 0.0000068505) = 0.000001 ;
 666   
 667   tssm(i,j,z)    = SUM[(comm,acts,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 668                        $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 669                        VMFP(comm,acts,reg)-VMFB(comm,acts,reg)];
 670   
 671   tssd(i,j,z)    = SUM[(comm,acts,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 672                        $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 673                        VDFP(comm,acts,reg)-VDFB(comm,acts,reg)];
 674   
 675  *==============================================================================
 676  * 2.4.5 Imports
 677  *==============================================================================
 678  * Imports are defined in GTAP at world prices (VCIF) and at market prices
 679  * (VMSB). Data on bilateral flows also include margins on imports (VTMFSD) and
 680  * import duties (TFRV). On the export side, the database includes exports at
 681  * market prices (VXSB), at world prices (VFOB) and subsidies on exports (MFRV
 682  * and XTRV).
 683  * The relationships between those variables is the following:
 684  *       VMSB = VCIF + TFRV
 685  *       VCIF = VFOB + VTMFSD
 686  *       VXSB = VFOB - MFRV - XTRV
 687  *
 688  * Imports are evaluated at world prices (VCIF) less transport margins (VTMFSD).
 689   
 690  ** Elimination of trade within a country:
 691  ** Trade within any entity that is a GTAP single-country region (or equivalent)
 692  ** is removed.
 693   VCIF(comm,z1c,z1c)        = 0;
 694   VTMFSD(marg,comm,z1c,z1c) = 0;
 695   
 696   IMO(i,zj,z)     = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 697                         $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 698                         VCIF(comm,regj,reg)-
 699                         SUM[marg,VTMFSD(marg,comm,regj,reg)]};
 700  *lt Strictly less than
 701   IMO(i,zj, z)$(IMO(i, zj, z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 702   IMO(i,zj,z)$sameas(zj,z) = 0 ;
 703   
 704  * IMO(i,zj,z)$(abs(IMO(i,zj,z)) < 1e-3) = 0;
 705  * IMO(i,zj,z)$sameas(zj,z) = 0 ;
 706   
 707  *==============================================================================
 708  * 2.4.6 Exports
 709  *==============================================================================
 710  *  To limit the sources of potential desequilibrium, exports are simply set
 711  *  equal to imports.
 712   
 713   EXO(i,zj,z)     = IMO(i,zj,z);
 714   EXTO(i,z)       = sum(zj, EXO(i,z,zj));
 715   
 716  * VXSB(comm,z1c,z1c)        = 0;
 717   
 718  * Alternative method bring the export value
 719  * EXO(i,zj,z)     = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 720  *                       $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 721  *                       VXSB(comm,regj,reg)};
 722  *
 723  *;
 724   
 725  * EXO(i,zj,z)$(abs(EXO(i,zj,z)) < 1e-8) = 1e-3;
 726  * EXTO(i,z)       = sum(zj, EXO(i,z,zj));
 727   
 728  *==============================================================================
 729  * 2.4.7 Margins
 730  *==============================================================================
 731  *  Transport margins are given by the variable VTMFSD
 732  * tmrg(TRP,ij,zj,z)$IMO(ij,zj,z)
 733  *                 = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[j2comm(ij,comm)
 734  *                       $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 735  *                       SUM[marg,VTMFSD(marg,comm,regj,reg)]};
 736   
 737   tmrg('20_LTRP',ij,zj,z)$IMO(ij,zj,z)
 738                   = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(ij,comm)
 739                         $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 740                         VTMFSD('otp',comm,regj,reg)};
 741   
 742   tmrg('20_LTRP',ij,zj,z)$(tmrg('20_LTRP',ij,zj,z)lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 743   
 744   tmrg('21_WTRP',ij,zj,z)$IMO(ij,zj,z)
 745                   = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(ij,comm)
 746                         $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 747                         VTMFSD('wtp',comm,regj,reg)};
 748   
 749   tmrg('21_WTRP',ij,zj,z)$(tmrg('21_WTRP',ij,zj,z)lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 750   
 751   tmrg('22_ATRP',ij,zj,z)$IMO(ij,zj,z)
 752                   = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(ij,comm)
 753                         $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 754                         VTMFSD('atp',comm,regj,reg)};
 755   
 756   tmrg('22_ATRP',ij,zj,z)$(tmrg('22_ATRP',ij,zj,z)lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 757   
 758   
 759  * Supply of transport margin are given by the variable VST
 760   MRGNO(i,z)      = SUM{(marg,reg)$[i2comm(i,marg)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 761                         VST(marg,reg)};
 762   
 763   MRGNO(i,z)$(MRGNO(i,z)lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 764   
 765  *==============================================================================
 766  * 2.4.8 Import duties
 767  *==============================================================================
 768  *  Import duties are given by the variable TFRV
 769   
 770   TIMO(i,zj,z)$IMO(i,zj,z)
 771                   = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 772                         $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 773                         TFRV(comm,regj,reg)};
 774   
 775  *==============================================================================
 776  * 2.4.9 Taxes on exports
 777  *==============================================================================
 778  *  Taxes on exports are given by the sum of MFRV and XTRV
 779   
 780   TIXO(i,z,zj)$IMO(i,z,zj)
 781                   = SUM{(comm,reg,regj)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 782                         $z2reg(z,reg)$z2reg(zj,regj)],
 783                         MFRV(comm,reg,regj)+XTRV(comm,reg,regj)};
 784   
 785  *==============================================================================
 786  * 2.4.10 Taxes on factors of production
 787  *==============================================================================
 788  * Net taxes on factor of production are calculated as taxes (FTRV)
 789  * less subsidies (FBEP).
 790   
 791   TIWO(l,j,z)      = SUM{(endw,acts,reg)$[f2endw(l,endw)
 792                         $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 793                         FTRV(endw,acts,reg)+
 794                         FBEP(endw,acts,reg)};
 795   
 796   TIWO_J(l,z)   = SUM(j, TIWO(l,j,z));
 797   
 798   TIKO(k,j,z)     = SUM{(endw,acts,reg)$[f2endw(k,endw)
 799                         $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 800                         FTRV(endw,acts,reg)+
 801                         FBEP(endw,acts,reg)};
 802   
 803   TIKO_J(k,z) = SUM(j, TIKO(k,j,z));
 804   
 805  *==============================================================================
 806  * 2.4.11 Taxes on production
 807  *==============================================================================
 808  * Taxes on production are set equal to the negative value of production
 809  * subsidies (OSEP).
 810   
 811   TIPO(j,z)       = SUM{(comm,reg)$[j2comm(j,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 812                         OSEP(comm,reg)};
 813   
 814  *==============================================================================
 815  * 2.4.12 Domestic taxes on commodities
 816  *==============================================================================
 817  * Domestic taxes on commodities are evaluated as the difference between
 818  * demand at agent prices and demand at market prices.
 819   
 820   TICO(i,z)       = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 821                        VDPP(comm,reg)-VDPB(comm,reg)
 822                       +VMPP(comm,reg)-VMPB(comm,reg)
 823                       +VDGP(comm,reg)-VDGB(comm,reg)
 824                       +VMGP(comm,reg)-VMGB(comm,reg)
 825                       +SUM[acts,VDFP(comm,acts,reg)
 826                            +VMFP(comm,acts,reg)]
 827   
 828                       -SUM[acts,VDFB(comm,acts,reg)
 829                             +VMFB(comm,acts,reg)]};
 830   
 831   
 832  *Balancing 2019
 833   
 834  TICO('04_GAS','06_PRK')   = TICO('04_GAS','06_PRK') -3.59655 -1.0;
 835  TICO('04_GAS','05_MNG')   = TICO('04_GAS','05_MNG') -2.15382 -1.0;
 836  TICO('03_OIL','05_MNG')   = TICO('03_OIL','05_MNG') -3.30004 -1.0;
 837  TICO('03_OIL','06_PRK')   = TICO('03_OIL','06_PRK') -2.13592 -1.0;
 838   
 839  *==============================================================================
 840  * 2.4.13 Direct taxes
 841  *==============================================================================
 842  * Direct taxes is given by the difference between factor payment at
 843  * market prices (EVFB) and endowment at agent prices (EVOS)
 844   
 845   TDHO(z)            = SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),
 846                         SUM[endw,SUM(acts,EVFB(endw,acts,reg))
 847                         -SUM(acts,EVOS(endw, acts, reg))]};
 848   
 849   DTAX(f,z)          = SUM{(endw,reg)$[f2endw(f,endw)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 850                         SUM[acts,EVFB(endw,acts,reg)] -
 851                         SUM[acts,EVOS(endw,acts, reg)]} ;
 852   
 853  *==============================================================================
 854  * 2.4.14 Factors of production
 855  *==============================================================================
 856  * Remuneration of the production factors is evaluated at market prices,
 857  * that is before taxes (EVFB).
 858   
 859   LDO(l,j,z)       = SUM{(endw,acts,reg)$[f2endw(l,endw)
 860                         $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 861                         EVFB(endw,acts,reg)};
 862   
 863   LDO(l,j,z)$(LDO(l,j,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 864   LDO_J(l,z)  = SUM(j,LDO(l,j,z)) - DTAX(l,z);
 865   
 866   RKDO(k,j,z)      = SUM{(endw,acts,reg)$[f2endw(k,endw)
 867                         $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 868                         EVFB(endw,acts,reg)};
 869   
 870   RKDO("cap",j,z)$(RKDO("cap",j,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 871   RKDO("natr","04_GAS","01_KOR")$(RKDO("natr","04_GAS","01_KOR") lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 872   RKDO("natr","04_GAS","05_MNG")$(RKDO("natr","04_GAS","05_MNG") lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 873   RKDO("natr","04_GAS","06_PRK")$(RKDO("natr","04_GAS","06_PRK") lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 874   RKDO("natr","05_MINING","06_PRK")$(RKDO("natr","05_MINING","06_PRK") lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 875   
 876  * Total capital stock at the beginning of the period
 877   KSTO(z)         = SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),VKB(reg)};
 878   
 879  *==============================================================================
 880  * 2.4.15 Depreciation
 881  *==============================================================================
 882  * Depreciation is given by the variable VDEP
 883   
 884   DEPO(z)         = SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),VDEP(reg)};
 885   
 886  *==============================================================================
 887  * 2.4.16 Population
 888  *==============================================================================
 889  *  Population by region
 890   POPO(z)         = SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),POP(reg)};
 891   
 892  *==============================================================================
 893  * 2.4.17 Domestic demand
 894  *==============================================================================
 895  * Once again, to avoid descrepencies, domestic purchases are calculated
 896  * by substracting imports, transport margins and indirect taxes from total
 897  * domestic absorption.
 898   
 899   DDO(i,z)        = CO(i,z)+CGO(i,z)+INVO(i,z)+SUM[j,DIO(i,j,z)]-TICO(i,z)
 900                     -SUM[zj,TIMO(i,zj,z)]-SUM[zj,IMO(i,zj,z)]
 901                     -SUM[(ij,zj),tmrg(ij,i,zj,z)];
 902   
 903  *==============================================================================
 904  * 2.4.18 MAKE Matrix
 905  *==============================================================================
 906   
 907   MAKE(j,i,z) = SUM[(acts,comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 908                        $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 909                        MAKEB(comm,acts,reg)];
 910   
 911  *==============================================================================
 912  * 2.5 Equilibrate data
 913  *==============================================================================
 914  *  2.5.1 Equilibrium on the world margin market
 915  *==============================================================================
 916  *  The first step would be to equilibrate international markets. As there is a
 917  *  small difference between supply of margins and demand, we chose to adjust
 918  *  the supply side by increasing or reducing each region's production
 919  *  proportionately.
 920   
 921   MRGNO(i,z)$MRGNO(i,z)
 922                   = MRGNO(i,z)*SUM[(ij,zj,zjj),tmrg(i,ij,zj,zjj)]
 923                    /SUM[zjj,MRGNO(i,zjj)];
 924   
 925  **==============================================================================
 926  * 2.5.2 Equilibrium in each region
 927  *==============================================================================
 928  *  As exports have already been set equal to imports, the remaining differences
 929  *  would appear in the national data. Total production is first set equal to
 930  *  the sum of production for the domestic market (DSO), adjusted production
 931  *  of margins (MRGNO) and exports.
 932   
 933   DSO_I(i,z)        = DDO(i,z) ;
 934   XSO_I(i,z)        = DDO(i,z)+MRGNO(i,z)+SUM[zj,EXO(i,z,zj)-TIXO(i,z,zj)];
 935   XSO(j,i,z)        = XSO_I(i,z)*[MAKE(j,i,z)/sum(jj,MAKE(jj,i,z))];
 936   XSTO(j,z)         = SUM(i, XSO(j,i,z));
 937   EXTO(i,z)         = SUM[zj,EXO(i,z,zj)];
 938   DSO(j,i,z)        = DDO(i,z)*[MAKE(j,i,z)/sum(jj,MAKE(jj,i,z))];
 939   
 940  *  The operating surplus is the variable that was used to equilibrate the
 941  *  regional data. As all other variables (income, savings and so on) will
 942  *  be calculated based on the variables described in these steps, there
 943  *  should not be any other descrepency.
 944   
 945  * for Data Balancing in 2019 Database
 946  TIPO('04_GAS','06_PRK')       = -9.19154 -0.1;
 947  TIPO('09_PAPERPRO','05_MNG')  = -7.77282  -0.1;
 948  TIPO('11_CHEMICAL','05_MNG')  = -7.2221  -0.809803 -0.1;
 949  TIPO('03_OIL','06_PRK')       = -6.11563 -0.1;
 950  TIPO('13_IRONSTL','05_MNG')   = -5.64578 -0.1;
 951  TIPO('19_eNuclear','06_PRK')  = -4.99124 -0.1;
 952  TIPO('23_eWind','06_PRK')     = -4.99122 -0.1;
 953  TIPO('24_eSolar','06_PRK')    = -4.92509 -0.1;
 954  TIPO('19_eNuclear','05_MNG')  = -4.81788 -0.1;
 955  TIPO('19_eNuclear','17_PAO')  = -4.80275 -0.1;
 956  TIPO('26_eOther','05_MNG')    = -4.80001 -0.1;
 957  TIPO('21_eGas','05_MNG')      = -4.78731 -0.1;
 958  TIPO('19_eNuclear','14_CPA')  = -4.63479 -0.1;
 959  TIPO('21_eGas','06_PRK')      = -4.12172 -0.1;
 960  TIPO('24_eSolar','14_CPA')    = -3.06953 -0.1;
 961  TIPO('26_eOther','06_PRK')    = -2.96659 -0.1;
 962  TIPO('14_NONFERR','06_PRK')   = -2.12762 -0.1;
 963  TIPO('10_PETROLCOAL','06_PRK')= -1.82929 -0.1;
 964  TIPO('24_eSolar','05_MNG')    = -0.654131 -0.1;
 965  TIPO('22_eOil','06_PRK')      = -0.408636 -0.1;
 966  TIPO('04_GAS','01_KOR')       = -0.00115488 -0.1;
 967  TIPO('04_GAS','05_MNG')       = -0.0039926 -7.1598 -0.1;
 968  TIPO('05_MINING','06_PRK ')   = -0.0394804 -0.1;
 969   
 970  * RKDO('cap',j,z)  = XSTO(j,z)-SUM[i,DIO(i,j,z)]-LDO(j,z)-TIWO(j,z)
 971  *                   -TIPO(j,z)-SUM[k,TIKO(k,j,z)]-RKDO('land',j,z) -RKDO('natr',j,z);
 972   
 973  RKDO('cap',j,z)  = XSTO(j,z)-SUM[i,DIO(i,j,z)]-SUM[l, LDO(l,j,z)+TIWO(l,j,z)]
 974                     -TIPO(j,z)-SUM[k,TIKO(k,j,z)]-RKDO('land',j,z) -RKDO('natr',j,z);
 975   
 976  RKDO_J(k,z) = sum(j,RKDO(k,j,z)) - DTAX(k,z);
 977   
 978  TotalCost(j,z) = SUM[i,DIO(i,j,z)]
 979                      +SUM[l,LDO(l,j,z)+TIWO(l,j,z)]
 980                      +TIPO(j,z)
 981                      +SUM[k,TIKO(k,j,z)+RKDO(k,j,z)];
 982   
 983  *==============================================================================
 984  * 3. CES elasticities
 985  *==============================================================================
 986  * 3.1 Definition of GTAP parameters
 987  *==============================================================================
 988  PARAMETER
 989   ESUBD(comm, reg)   Elasticity of substitution between domestic product and imports
 990   ESUBM(comm, reg)   Elasticity of substitution between imports from different regions
 991   ESUBVA(acts, reg)  Elasticity of substitution between primary factors in the production of value added
 992   ELFKLE(acts, reg)  Elasticity of substitution between VA-energy sub-production
 993   
 994  *==============================================================================
 995  * 3.2 Definition in PEP w
 996  *==============================================================================
 997   sigma_M1(i,z)   Elasticity (CES - composite commodity)
 998   sigma_M2(i,z)   Elasticity (CES - composite import)
 999   sigma_VA(j,z)   Elasticity (CES - value added)
1000   sigma_KLE(j,z)  Elastcitiy (CES - KL-E)
1001   
1002  *==============================================================================
1003  * 3.3 Temporary variables
1004  *==============================================================================
1005   IM_GTAP(comm,z)  Total imports using the GTAP commodity sets
1006   Q_GTAP(comm,z)   Composite commodity using the GTAP commodity sets
1007   VA_GTAP(acts,z)  Value added using the GTAP sectors
1008   KLE_GTAP(acts,z) KLE using the GTAP sectors
1009   E_GTAP(acts,z)   E using ther GTAP sectors
1010   SH_IM(comm,i,z)  Share of each import TRAD_COM in aggregation i for region z
1011   SH_Q(comm,i,z)   Share of each composite commodity TRAD_COM in aggregation i for region z
1012   SH_VA(acts,j,z)  Share of each sector TRAD_COM in aggregation j for region z
1013   SH_KLE(acts,j,z) Share of each sector KLE in aggregation j for region z
1014  ;
1015   
1016  *==============================================================================
1017  * 3.4 Load the GTAP file which includes the parameters
1018  *==============================================================================
GDXIN   C:\Users\kimc0\GUIDE_GLOBAL_CGE\4.SAM\Input_w-t\GTAP11c_Parameters2019.gdx
--- LOAD  ESUBD = 19:ESUBD
--- LOAD  ESUBM = 20:ESUBM
--- LOAD  ESUBVA = 61:ESUBVA
--- LOAD  ELFKLE = 62:ELFKLE
1021   
1022  *==============================================================================
1023  *  3.5 sigma_M1
1024  *==============================================================================
1025  * Elasticities of substitution between domestic product and imports are
1026  * aggregated acording to the share of each commodity (QO) TRAD_COMM in total I
1027   
1028   Q_GTAP(comm,z)
1029                   = SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),
1030                     VDPP(comm,reg)+VMPP(comm,reg)+
1031                     VDGP(comm,reg)+VMGP(comm,reg)+
1032                     VDIP(comm,reg)+VMIP(comm,reg)+
1033                     SUM[acts,VDFP(comm,acts,reg)+
1034                         VMFP(comm,acts,reg)]};
1035   
1036   
1037   SH_Q(comm,i,z)$i2comm(i,comm)
1038                   = Q_GTAP(comm,z)/
1039                     SUM{commi$i2comm(i,commi),
1040                         Q_GTAP(commi,z)};
1041   
1042   sigma_M1(i,z)   = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1043                     ESUBD(comm,reg)*SH_Q(comm,i,z)};
1044   
1045  *==============================================================================
1046  *  3.6 sigma_M2
1047  *==============================================================================
1048  * Elasticities of substitution between imports from different partners are
1049  * aggregated acording to the share of total import (IMTO) TRAD_COMM in total I
1050   
1051   IM_GTAP(comm,z)
1052                   = SUM[regj,SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),VCIF(comm,regj,reg)}];
1053   
1054   SH_IM(comm,i,z)$i2comm(i,comm)
1055                   = IM_GTAP(comm,z)/
1056                     SUM{commi$i2comm(i,commi),
1057                         IM_GTAP(commi,z)};
1058   
1059   sigma_M2(i,z)   = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1060                     ESUBM(comm,reg)*SH_IM(comm,i,z)};
1061   
1062  *==============================================================================
1063  *  3.7 sigma_VA
1064  *==============================================================================
1065  * Elasticities of substitution between factors of production are aggregated
1066  * acording to the share of each sector (VA) TRAD_COMM in total I
1067   
1068   VA_GTAP(acts,z)
1069                   = SUM{endw,
1070                         SUM[reg$z2reg(z,reg),EVFB(endw,acts,reg)]};
1071   
1072   SH_VA(acts,j,z)$j2acts(j,acts)
1073                   = VA_GTAP(acts,z)/
1074                     SUM{actsj$j2acts(j,actsj),
1075                         VA_GTAP(actsj,z)};
1076   
1077   sigma_VA(j,z)   = SUM{(acts,reg)$[j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1078                     ESUBVA(acts,reg)*SH_VA(acts,j,z)};
1079   
1080  *==============================================================================
1081  *  3.8 sigma_KLE
1082  *==============================================================================
1083   KLE_GTAP(acts,z)
1084                   = SUM{endw,
1085                         SUM[reg$z2reg(z,reg),EVFB(endw,acts,reg)]} +
1086                       SUM[i,
1087                          SUM[(comm,reg)$[i2comm2(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1088                               VDFP(comm,acts,reg)+VMFP(comm,acts,reg)]];
1089   
1090   E_GTAP(acts,z)
1091                   = SUM[i,
1092                          SUM[(comm,reg)$[i2comm2(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1093                               VDFP(comm,acts,reg)+VMFP(comm,acts,reg)]];
1094   
1095   SH_KLE(acts,j,z)$j2acts(j,acts)
1096                   = KLE_GTAP(acts,z)/
1097                     SUM{actsj$j2acts(j,actsj),
1098                         KLE_GTAP(actsj,z)};
1099   
1100   sigma_KLE(j,z)   = SUM{(acts,reg)$[j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1101                      ELFKLE(acts, reg)*SH_KLE(acts,j,z)};
1102   
1103  *==============================================================================
1104  * 4. Own price elasticities (Conditional)
1105  *==============================================================================
1106  PARAMETER
1107   E_Composite(j,z)      E nest susbtitution elasticies
1108   KLE_Composite(j,z)    KLE nest susbtitution elasticies
1109   elas_E(j,z)           Own price elasticities(Composite Energy)
1110   elas_elec(j,z)        Own price elasticities(electricity)
1111   elas_gas(j,z)         Own price elasticities(gas)
1112   elas_oil(j,z)         Own price elasticities(oil)
1113   elas_coal(j,z)        Own price elasticities(coal)
1114   elas_petrolcoal(j,z)  Own price elasticities(petrolcoal)
1115  ;
1116   
1117   E_Composite(j,z)   = SUM{(acts)$[j2acts(j,acts)], E_GTAP(acts,z)};
1118   KLE_Composite(j,z) = SUM{(acts)$[j2acts(j,acts)], KLE_GTAP(acts,z)};
1119   
1120   elas_E(j,z) = sigma_KLE(j,z)*(1- E_Composite(j,z)/KLE_Composite(j,z));
1121   elas_elec(j,z) = 1.1*(1- DIO('18_ELEC',j,z)/E_Composite(j,z));
1122   elas_gas(j,z) = 1.1*(1- DIO('04_GAS',j,z)/E_Composite(j,z));
1123   elas_oil(j,z) = 1.1*(1- DIO('03_OIL',j,z)/E_Composite(j,z));
1124   elas_coal(j,z) = 1.1*(1- DIO('02_COAL',j,z)/E_Composite(j,z));
1125   elas_petrolcoal(j,z) = 1.1*(1- DIO('10_PETROLCOAL',j,z)/E_Composite(j,z));
1126   
1127  *==============================================================================
1128  * Projections used in Recursive Dynamic model
1129  *==============================================================================
1130  PARAMETER
1131   ACT_POP(z,time)         Active population from 1980 to 2050 based on the PEP w aggregation
1132  * ACT_POP_GTAP8(reg,time) Active population from 1980 to 2050 based on the GTAP8 aggregation
1133   CAB_Foure(z,time)       Implicit CAB in Foure et al projections
1134   exogro(z,time)          Exogenous growth factor for exogenously growing variables
1135   exogro_LS(z,time)       Exogenous growth factor for exogenously growing labor supply
1136   g_GDP(z,time)           GDP growth
1137   g_KS(z,time)            Capital stock growth rate
1138   g_LS(z,time)            Active population growth rate
1139   g_POP(z,time)           Population growth rate
1140   g_SDR(z,time)           Domestic savings rate growth rate
1141   GDP(z,time)             GDP projection based on the PEP w aggregation
1142  * GDP_GTAP8(reg,time)     GDP from 1980 to 2050 based on the GTAP8 aggregation
1143   gdp_per_cap(z)          GDP per capita
1144   I_rate(z,time)          Investment rate - domestic savings over GDP
1145   Invest(z,time)          Investments from 1980 to 2050 based on PEP w aggregation
1146  * Invest_GTAP8(reg,time)  Investments from 1980 to 2050 based on GTAP8 aggregation
1147  * K_Stock_GTAP8(reg,time) Capital stock from 1980 to 2050 based on the GTAP8 aggregation
1148   K_Stock(z,time)         Capital stock from 1980 to 2050 based on the PEP w aggregation
1149   TFP(z,time)             Total factor productivity index 1980-2050 for PEP w aggregation
1150  * TFP_GTAP8(reg,time)     Total factor productivity 1980-2050 for GTAP8 aggregation
1151   S_rate(z,time)          Savings rate - domestic savings over GDP
1152   Savings(z,time)         Domestic savings from 1980 to 2050 based on PEP w aggregation
1153  * Savings_GTAP8(reg,time) Domestic savings from 1980 to 2050 based on GTAP8 aggregation
1154   sdr_fac(z,time)         Exogenous change factor for domestic savings rate
1155   TOT_POP(z,time)         Total population from 1980 to 2050 based on the PEP w aggregation
1156  * TOT_POP_GTAP8(reg,time) Total population from 1980 to 2050 based on the GTAP8 aggregation
1157   CTAX_Cal(z,time)        Carbon Tax for Baseline Scenario
1158   CTAX_CPS(z,time)        Carbon Tax for Current Policy Scenario
1159   CTAX_NZS(z,time)        Carbon Tax for Net-Zero Scenario
1160   EMPLOY(j,z)             Employment by sector 2019 (thousand)
1161   AEEI_low(z,time)        Autonomous energy efficiency improvement
1162   AEEI_high(z,time)       Autonomous energy efficiency improvement
1163   TREND(z,time)           Value to Physical quantity
1164   TREND2(z,time)          Value to Physical quantity
1165   TREND_CPS(z,time)       Value to Physical quantity
1166   TREND_NZS(z,time)       Value to Physical quantity
1167   PERMIT_Cal(z,time)      PERMIT
1168   
1169  ;
1170   
GDXIN   C:\Users\kimc0\GUIDE_GLOBAL_CGE\4.SAM\Input_w-t\Projection.gdx
--- LOAD  GDP = 1:GDP
--- LOAD  TOT_POP = 2:TOT_POP
--- LOAD  g_SDR = 3:g_SDR
--- LOAD  AEEI_low = 4:AEEI_low
--- LOAD  AEEI_high = 5:AEEI_high
--- LOAD  TREND = 6:TREND
--- LOAD  TREND2 = 7:TREND2
